  6. THE SIBLING LADDER: the residual measured against how many siblings the removed electron had

     Every corridor row is an INNER-SHELL removal the store carries as a later ionisation limit of
     the neutral, so the electron leaves a shell that still holds siblings.  Sibling energy is the
     converged second-order pair correlation it loses (siblingpair.py, LMAX = 5).

     row     el  siblings   predicted   measured   residual        sibling E   undelivered
     3p      Al       0       5.999      5.986   +0.00050 Ha    0.00000           -
     4d      Y        0       6.114      6.217   -0.00381 Ha    0.00000           -
     4p      Ga       0       6.013      5.999   +0.00052 Ha    0.00000           -
     5d      La       0       6.415      6.494   -0.00290 Ha    0.00000           -
     5p      In       0       5.800      5.786   +0.00052 Ha    0.00000           -
     6p      Tl       0       6.061      6.108   -0.00174 Ha    0.00000           -
     C:2s    B        1      12.816     12.927   -0.00407 Ha    0.01683       0.242
     C:3s    Al       1      10.551     10.622   -0.00260 Ha    0.01793       0.145
     C:4s    Ga       1      11.399     11.872   -0.01740 Ha    0.01662       1.047
     C:2p    Na       5      37.716     37.986   -0.00990 Ha    0.09138       0.108
     C:5p    Xe       5      12.163     12.130   +0.00121 Ha    0.06629       0.018
     C:5d    Hg       9      14.349     14.841   -0.01806 Ha    0.09032       0.200
     4f      Yb      13       5.878      8.909   -0.11141 Ha    0.16664       0.669

     6 OF 7 CORRIDOR ROWS SIT WITHIN 0.018 Ha, and so does every zero-sibling opening (0.0038 Ha at worst).
     Yb ALONE IS 0.111 Ha -- 6 times the next largest, which is Hg at -0.0181.
     The undelivered fraction runs from 0.018 at Xe to 1.047 at Ga with no order in sibling
     count, sibling energy or <r>, so there is no measured law that converts a sibling count into
     a correction, and a transfer built on Yb's fraction alone has no support.  What the
     ladder gives is a BOUND: |residual| <= 0.018 Ha, and inside the zero-sibling band
     of +-0.004 Ha at two of the three one-sibling rows.

     Ga carries the largest one-sibling residual, -0.0174 Ha, and has a named reason: its 4s sits
     directly above a filled 3d10, so the removal carries a d-shell relaxation none of the
     other one-sibling rows do.  It is not the ladder's worst row -- that is the line above.

